> emptyhanded - one Samurai of mine has already died because of this
> dumbness.  What do I do?

I don't know if you can twoweapon in polymorphed form, perhaps someone
else will help you here.

Anyway, the easies way to start twoweaponing is to first set the
"pushweapon" option to true. Next, wield the weapon that you want to be
your secondary weapon. Then, wield your primary weapon. The other weapon
now automatically becomes your secondary (spare) weapon.

Once you have a primary weapon and a secondary (not wielded) weapon, you
can issue the "#twoweapon" command.

Note most character classes cannot twoweapon. Also, it is advisable to
first practice with single weapon combat, to advance your skill in the
individual weapons before you start to twoweapon.

> Also, I've been cheating a bit like this;

Don't cheat. It will get you nowhere: it's disastrous for your playing
skills. As any experienced player will tell you, they only started to
become good at the game when they stopped cheating. Read this newsgroup's
FAQ before asking any more questions. Specifically, read questions 4.1,
4.2 and 4.3.

> Is this a part of the bone file code?  Is there any way I can stop
> it!?

There's only a 1/3 chance that a bones level will be read, and when you
don't die on that same level, the bones file is deleted (you can only get
bones on the level you die on). So if you enter the level, leave it
immediately again, and die somewhere else, it's gone.

> Also, how do I get new pets?

Throw a food item that a cat or dog or horse likes to a hostile one if you
encounter it. For a cat/dog, this includes tripe, or food rations or
something else meaty, while horses and ponies like vegetables and fruit.

Other creatures cannot be tamed by throwing them food: you need magical
means for those (spell or scroll of taming among other means).

